name: governance-gate

# Trigger: a pull-request event type that runs the DEFAULT branch's copy of this workflow,
# on opened, reopened, synchronize (new head) and edited (body changes). Which trigger puts
# the result on the PR head as the required check is the delivery's to verify.
# Permissions: read contents and pull requests; nothing else.

# Job `governance-gate` (the required check name):
#
# 1. Check out the default branch only. Never check out or run the PR's code.
# 2. Read `.github/governance/record.yml` from that checkout.
# 3. Author: the PR author is habit or the agent account, else fail
#    ("outside PRs are re-landed").
# 4. Risk line: exactly one body line `Risk: low|medium|high — <reason>`, else fail.
# 5. Pure revert: if the body has `Reverts: <sha>`, fetch the PR head and merge-base as git
#    objects, recompute the revert of <sha> on the merge-base, and compare trees with the
#    head. Identical: pass at any declared tier and skip step 6. Different: continue.
# 6. Floor: list the PR's changed files; match each against the default and confirmed
#    sensitive paths; the declared tier must be at least the highest matching floor.
# 7. Report each failure as one plain line naming the rule and the fix.
